    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "character value, so that $q = 0.012$. Expressing this in the form used by Table 11.1 gives prb(0.012) = prb(0.5 - 0.488) = -prb(0.5 + 0.488) = -2.25. Zero on the probit scale corresponds to the population median ($q = 0.50$), which is also the mean for a normal. For a normally distributed variable, a unit change on the probit scale corresponds to one standard deviation (Figure 11.2).",
      "source_page": 311,
