      "content": "with multimodal, overly peaked, and skewed distributions all exhibiting characteristic departures (Figure 11.3). The normal probability scale forms the basis for the most powerful tests for departures from normality, such as the small-sample W test of Shapiro and Wilk (1965) and the large-sample D test of D'Agostino (1971).",
